{"path":"\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/' data-target='root' data-title=''>&#8962; <\/a>\r\n\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer' data-target='computer' data-title='Computer'>\r\n\t\t\tComputer\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os' data-target='computer\/os' data-title='OS'>\r\n\t\t\tOS\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n","async":"0","desc":"Windows notes: setup, shell, registry, networking, partitions, and fixes across XP through 10 and Server 2008.","label":"Windows","prevArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/nix","label":"*Nix","url":"\/computer\/os\/nix"},"nextArticle":null,"languageSwitcher":"<div id='language-switcher'>\n<\/div>\n","content":"<div id='message'>\n\t\t<div class='content-image-container'>\r\n\t<div class='cover-image cover-image-tile'>\r\n\t\t<img src='\/computer\/os\/windows.svg' alt='Windows notes: setup, shell, registry, networking, partitions, and fixes across XP through 10 and Server 2008.' style='object-fit: contain; object-position: center'>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<p class='cover-credit'>\n\t<span class='cover-credit-anchor'>\n\t\t<button type='button' class='cover-credit-toggle' aria-expanded='false' aria-label='Image credit'>\n\t\t\t<svg xmlns='http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg' viewBox='0 0 16 16' width='14' height='14' aria-hidden='true' focusable='false'>\n\t\t\t\t<circle cx='8' cy='8' r='6.25' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.2'\/>\n\t\t\t\t<circle cx='8' cy='5.2' r='0.85' fill='currentColor'\/>\n\t\t\t\t<path fill='currentColor' d='M7.28 7.15h1.44v4.55H7.28z'\/>\n\t\t\t<\/svg>\n\t\t<\/button>\n\t\t<span class='cover-credit-popup'><a class=\"content-link cover-credit-link\" href=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/File%3AWindows_11_logo.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft<\/a> \/ <a class=\"content-link cover-credit-link\" href=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/File%3AWindows_11_logo.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a> \u2014 <span>Public domain<\/span><\/span>\n\t<\/span>\n<\/p>\n\n\t<h2 class='center'>Windows notes: setup, shell, registry, networking, partitions, and fixes across XP through 10 and Server 2008.<\/h2>\n\t\t<p>\n\t\tWindows notes: setup, shell, registry, networking, partitions, and fixes across XP through 10 and Server 2008.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Topics<\/h2>\n\t<ul class=\"list-bullet content-list\">\n\t\t<li><div><strong>ACL<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Ad hoc Wi-Fi<\/strong> \u2014 Use an elevated command prompt.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Autostart<\/strong> \u2014 Run <code class='inline'>TaskSched.msc<\/code>. From the Action pane, click <strong>Create Task\u2026<\/strong>.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Bash<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Command Shell<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Customization<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>dir<\/strong> \u2014 List files recursively with dir \/A:-DR \/S.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>EFS<\/strong> \u2014 A certificate without the private key can be used for Read-Only.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Enable AHCI<\/strong> \u2014 Enable safe mode.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Environment variable<\/strong> \u2014 Variables management box.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Explorer<\/strong> \u2014 Opens a new window in single-paned (My Computer) view for each item selected, even if the new window duplicates a window that is already open.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>File Sharing<\/strong> \u2014 Directories which are accessible as per the present credential automatically become visible.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Firewall<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Hidden Partition<\/strong> \u2014 In diskpart, a hidden partition reports Id 27 and Type Hidden. Set the ID and assign a drive letter.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Hide Folder<\/strong> \u2014 Rename the folder and redirect it to the Recycle Bin namespace by giving it this suffix.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Install<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>RunAsSystem and RunFromToken<\/strong> \u2014 Joakim's RunFromToken and RunAsSystem tools.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Key<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Language Codes<\/strong> \u2014 List of language codes.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>License<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Migrate to SSD<\/strong> \u2014 Repair the EFI bootloader after migrating Windows to an SSD. Walkthrough.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Monitor Power Management<\/strong> \u2014 - <code class='inline'>1<\/code> \u2014 the display is going to low power. - <code class='inline'>2<\/code> \u2014 the display is being shut off. - <code class='inline'>-1<\/code> \u2014 the display is being turned on (undocumented value).<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>MSI<\/strong> \u2014 The GUID has dashes.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>10<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>7<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>8<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Navigation Pane<\/strong> \u2014 Add a path at root level to Explorer.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>NET<\/strong> \u2014 Caution: creating accounts and changing group membership needs admin rights.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Network<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Partitions<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Power Management<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Prepare USB Media for OS Installation<\/strong> \u2014 Prepare USB media to install Windows.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Prevent Password Change<\/strong> \u2014 Caution: this changes account policy and needs admin rights.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>ReadyBoost<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Recovery<\/strong> \u2014 A recovery partition is required for Resetting. <code class='inline'>Winre.wim<\/code> is required to build a recovery drive.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Redistributables<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Registry<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Remote Assistance<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Remote Desktop<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Remote PowerShell<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Remote Registry<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Reset Password<\/strong> \u2014 Reset a local password from the recovery console by swapping the on-screen keyboard for <code class='inline'>cmd.exe<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Robocopy<\/strong> \u2014 - <code class='inline'>b<\/code> \u2014 BackUp Mode. No Access Denied. For BackUp Rights. - <code class='inline'>mir<\/code> \u2014 Mirror. - <code class='inline'>xJ<\/code> \u2014 Do not follow Junctions. - <code class='inline'>copyAll<\/code> \u2014 equivalent to <code class='inline'>\/COPY:DATSOU<\/code> (Data, Attrib, TimeStamps, Security, Owner, aUditing-Info). - <code class='inline'>xD<\/code> \u2014 Exclude Directory. - <code class='inline'>xF<\/code> \u2014 Exclude File.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Run<\/strong> \u2014 Register a Run-dialog command with AppPath.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>SC<\/strong> \u2014 Services ?creator?.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Search<\/strong> \u2014 Can be combined with a file match filter.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Server 2008<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Shortcut<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>SSD Settings<\/strong> \u2014 CU, LU: <code class='inline'>Temp<\/code>, <code class='inline'>Tmp<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Start<\/strong> \u2014 Bit flags for each processor. Example: <code class='inline'>(11)b<\/code> = <code class='inline'>(3)d<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Start Menu<\/strong> \u2014 Exit Explorer.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Symlink<\/strong> \u2014 Path is relative to <code class='inline'>&lt;target&gt;<\/code>.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Symlink Relative Paths<\/strong> \u2014 Relative symlinks' relativity is to their current location. This is to be considered in the creation command param.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>System Account CMD<\/strong> \u2014 Caution: this opens a command prompt as System. Admin rights.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Taskbar<\/strong> \u2014 User-pinned taskbar shortcuts live under %APPDATA%\\\\Microsoft\\\\Internet Explorer\\\\Quick Launch\\\\User Pinned\\\\TaskBar.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Telnet<\/strong> \u2014 <code class='inline'>-o<\/code> opens a host.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Time Auto Update<\/strong> \u2014 NTP uses UDP 123.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Touch<\/strong> \u2014 Stamp <code class='inline'>LastWriteTime<\/code> to the current time.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Unhide Folder<\/strong> \u2014 Recursive, directories included.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Uninstall Tool<\/strong> \u2014 Microsoft KB 290301 for the Windows uninstall tool.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Update<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>WSL<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>XBox<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>XP<\/strong><\/div><\/li>\n\t<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<div id='updated-container'>\r\n\t<div id='updated'>\r\n\t\tUpdated:\r\n\t\t<span id='date'>\r\n\t\t\t2026 Aug 19\t\t<\/span>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div class='center' id='content-body-separator'><\/div>\r\n<div id='sub-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n<a\r\n\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/acl' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/acl' data-title='ACL'>\r\n<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt=\"Navigation - link to computer\/os\/windows\/acl\"><div class='item_block_text'